## Ownership and memory

### Default moves

- Pass **owned** data forward when a stage consumes it; borrow when multiple readers need the same snapshot.
- **`clone` is a design smell** in hot paths — if you clone constantly, restructure ownership or use arenas/handles.

### Buffers and allocation

- **`Vec::with_capacity`** when upper bound is known (token count, section size).
- **Reuse buffers** (`clear()` + refill) in lexer/serializer loops instead of allocating per token.
- **Bulk allocation** (arenas) for many same-lifetime objects — one allocation, drop entire arena at once. Do not `Box` every AST/IR node individually when an arena fits the lifetime.

### `std::mem` helpers

- `take` / `replace` to move out of `&mut T` when you need owned value without cloning.
- `size_of`, `align_of`, and layout docs when defining bytecode or VM value layouts.

### Aliasing

- **`&mut` is exclusive** — do not hold other references to the same data while `&mut` is live.
- In `unsafe`, document **who may read/write** and for how long.

